cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this project and the upstream manuscript. This is a conditional
  research draft; include the repository commit used until a release is archived.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Zhihao
    alias: jacklightChen
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Exact certificates, source patches and research notes for conditional
  improvements to OpenAI's integer-multiplication manuscript. A ternary
  five-subset interchange motif and paired complex producer, composed with
  compact controls and fast Gaussian resampling, support kappa = 373/10^11
  greater than 2^-28. The upstream theorem and retained analytic interfaces
  are assumed; the new arguments are not independently reviewed or formally
  verified. Prior and AI-assisted contributions are detailed in NOTICE.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Integer multiplication below n log n"
    authors:
      - name: OpenAI
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/openai/math/tree/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Integer-multiplication-below-n-log-n-September-23-2026"
